      "content": "An eighth-century Latin copy of what is probably a second-century list —\nthe oldest surviving inventory of which books counted. It is damaged, it\nstarts mid-sentence, and it is missing the beginning.\n\nOur earliest evidence about what was canonical is itself a fragment\nsomebody happened to keep.",
